    "caveats": [
      "ABI4/5/6 reuse alignment-pair storage at first launch; alignment CCR4 pairing is retained, but its paired raw records are replaced.",
      "ABI5/6 preserve two checkpoints near second-alignment end: B minus (A+C)/2, not drive directed margin. Bit0 uses the alignment readout-window screen.",
      "alignment_hook_max_us includes selected alignment/pair work; stored with a65535-cycle ceiling. Neither maximum is a whole-ISR measurement.",
      "ABI6: first2ms of each of the two drive vectors at full consumed rate, otherwise one in four groups; ACCEPT always retained.512 records or61ms, skipped count explicit.",
      "Software ADC-readout timestamps and current timer register snapshots, not hardware sample times or an oscilloscope waveform.",
      "Blank/invalid groups remain visible. Flags bit0 is software-valid nonblank, not independent physical validity.",
      "Hook maximum covers selected recorder work only; excludes eligibility, detector, IRQ and launch header reset. No guarantee of unchanged timing."
    ]
